cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this white paper, please cite it as below."
title: "OneDrum: Server-Certified Rhythm Performance Scoring"
abstract: >-
  How OneDrum certifies human timing on consumer devices whose clocks lie:
  an audible clock carried by the media itself, calibration with no
  calibration step, in-play drift re-centring, an anti-spoof gate computed on
  calibration-invariant residuals, and an HMAC-signed score that any third
  party can verify. Every mechanism described is running in production and is
  backed by field data from 1,234 genuine attempts across desktop, iPhone,
  and Android.
type: report
